Hyprlume is available under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Hyprlume uses hyprpilot-core from HyprPilot (MIT OR Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/sumerchoudhary78/HyprPilot

Local speech inference uses sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) and ONNX Runtime (MIT):
https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

Native wireless adapters use nmrs 3.5.12 (MIT) and BlueR 0.17.4
(BSD-2-Clause, with separately attributed assigned-number data). Their full
upstream notices are retained in docs/third-party/ and installed with the docs:
https://github.com/freedesktop-rs/nmrs
https://github.com/bluez/bluer
libdbus is a dynamically linked system library and is installed separately.

Quickshell/Qt and espeak-ng are separately installed programs. Their licenses
apply to those programs. Hyprlume does not link espeak-ng or piper-phonemize.

Speech weights are not included in this repository or package. The opt-in
model installer downloads upstream archives, verifies pinned SHA-256 digests,
and retains upstream model cards and attribution. Model licenses remain
independent of Hyprlume's source license.

Desktop visual assets
---------------------
Caldera, First Light, Tidal Eclipse, the observatory backdrop and the transparent assistant are
generated project assets.

The bundled Instrument Serif Regular typeface is copyright 2022 The Instrument Serif
Project Authors and licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The original
notice and license are in shell/assets/fonts/instrument-serif/OFL.txt.
Prompts and origins are documented in shell/assets/README.md and docs/design/.
The original globe asset uses public-domain Natural Earth land geometry.
Installed runtime packages retain their own licenses.
